[driver] {'event': 'iteration_end', 'iteration': 2, 'attempt': 1, 'returncode': 0, 'tail': "ranking objective untouched), with the target expressed as the row's play ratio percentile *within its own duration bucket* — the diagnostic confirms `corr(target, dur_bucket) = −0.000` vs `−0.376` for the un-normalised form.\n\nBefore running, I finite-difference verified the aux head's gradients (V, Wa, ca, ba) in float64 and showed `rank_step` is bit-identical to the banked `listwise.infonce_step`, so the control arm is a true control.\n\n| Arm | valid | Δ vs control | test |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| R31-ctrl FM-rich, no aux | 0.61715 | — | 0.6098 ± 0.0010 |\n| R31a within-bucket, λ=0.3 | 0.61587 | −0.00128 | 0.6095 ± 0.0009 |\n| R31b within-bucket, λ=1.0 | 0.61608 | −0.00107 | 0.6095 ± 0.0002 |\n| R31c global percentile, λ=0.3 | 0.61584 | −0.00131 | 0.6095 ± 0.0009 |\n\nEvery aux arm is *below* the control on validation, so the pre-committed promotion step did not fire and nothing was banked. The magnitude is under the 0.002 bar so I claim no effect size, but the sign is consistent across 3 arms × 3 seeds and both metric components, which I recorded as a directional observation.\n\nThe informative result is R31c: a target with zero duration correlation and one with −0.376 perform *identically*, so duration mediation was Run 1's symptom rather than its cause — watch-completion is simply a different ordering of the same rows than within-user preference. The auxiliary-head family is now 0-for-2 (Run 19 sparse binary, Run 31 dense graded) for the same underlying reason. Also worth noting for the audit: the control reproduces Run 30's control to 5 dp on validation from an independently built code path.\n\nIDEAS.md, RESULTS.md and LOG.jsonl updated; committed and pushed as `49a2192`. Remaining OPEN: #13 K=2 under FM-rich, #14 per-field embedding sizes.\n\nITERATION RESULT: R31 play-ratio auxiliary head | 0.6095 | NOT_BANKED | Dense graded watch-completion supervision hurts the shared embeddings whether duration-normalised or not — Run 1's duration mediation was a symptom, not the cause.\n", 'ts': '2026-08-30 01:20:13'}
