[driver] {'event': 'iteration_end', 'iteration': 3, 'attempt': 1, 'returncode': 0, 'tail': "Iteration complete. Run 32 tested IDEAS #14 (per-field embedding sizes) as a per-field-pair *interaction rank* experiment — a 2×3 grid with a same-run control, with the masked training step asserted bit-identical to the banked one before any arm ran.\n\n| Arm | valid | Δ ctrl | test |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ctrl wide16/narrow16 | 0.61715 | — | 0.6098 |\n| a wide24/narrow8 (#14 as proposed) | 0.61098 | −0.00617 | 0.6046 |\n| b wide16/narrow8 | 0.61186 | −0.00529 | 0.6052 |\n| c wide24/narrow16 | 0.61568 | −0.00147 | 0.6092 |\n| d wide24/narrow24 | 0.61656 | −0.00059 | 0.6098 |\n\nThe proposed configuration is the worst of the five, and the result inverts the hypothesis in an informative way: the score tracks the **narrow** rank and ignores the wide one. Cutting narrow fields to rank 8 costs −0.0053 at unchanged wide rank (2.6× the gate, visible in both GAUC and nDCG@5), because `min(k_j, k_l)` means a narrow field's rank caps `prev1 × user_id` — a 3 × 26,210 surface. The causal sequence fields earn their Run 21 gain by modulating the user/video embeddings, so low cardinality is not low expressive load. Uniform k=24 ≈ k=16 also reconfirms Run 4's capacity saturation two premises later. Promotion did not fire; RESULTS.md, IDEAS.md and the log are updated and pushed. IDEAS #13 (K=2) is the last untested backlog item.\n\nITERATION RESULT: Run 32 per-field embedding sizes (interaction rank) | 0.6046 (best arm; control 0.6098) | NOT_BANKED | Per-field k is interaction rank, and the binding constraint is the NARROW fields, not the wide ones — narrow rank 8 costs −0.005 while wide rank 24 buys nothing.\n", 'ts': '2026-08-30 01:39:45'}
